1
00:00:01,969 --> 00:00:03,289
NARRATOR:
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:05,772 --> 00:00:07,584
ALFRED: <i>Taking a life will
lead you down a darker path</i>

3
00:00:07,608 --> 00:00:09,008
<i>that you could never imagine.</i>

4
00:00:09,476 --> 00:00:11,035
I know, I've been down it.

5
00:00:11,211 --> 00:00:12,873
I'm not the hero Gotham needs.

6
00:00:13,647 --> 00:00:16,242
ALFRED: <i>Then it's gonna
be a long, bumpy journey back.</i>

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,518
<i>You've met Martin, I see.</i>

8
00:00:21,588 --> 00:00:23,819
You and I, we're
more than friends.

9
00:00:24,258 --> 00:00:25,692
<i>We're conspirators.</i>

10
00:00:30,464 --> 00:00:31,693
Oh, no.

11
00:00:34,501 --> 00:00:36,527
<i>You are relieved of
duty, Harvey Bullock.</i>

12
00:00:36,637 --> 00:00:39,732
As of this moment, I am assuming
the captaincy of Gotham Central.

13
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,741
What did you
have to do to get it?

14
00:00:44,411 --> 00:00:47,677
NEWSREADER: <i>Gotham finds itself
in the hands of a ritualistic cop killer</i>

15
00:00:47,748 --> 00:00:49,273
<i>Being called Professor Pyg.</i>

16
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:54,847
THE PYG: <i>It doesn't stop until
I've butchered every single swine</i>

17
00:00:55,022 --> 00:00:57,082
<i>on Penguin's payroll.</i>

18
00:00:58,125 --> 00:00:59,286
I'm gonna find you.

19
00:00:59,393 --> 00:01:02,261
I hope you do, it's a spectacle.

20
00:01:04,498 --> 00:01:07,366
And you're my
muse, Jimmy Gordon.

21
00:01:09,069 --> 00:01:11,537
My poor lost lambs.

22
00:01:11,872 --> 00:01:15,502
I come to you today with
an offer for this evening.

23
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:20,279
Fresh biscuits and a
hearty bowl of soup.

24
00:01:20,814 --> 00:01:24,046
I have place settings for six.

25
00:01:26,553 --> 00:01:28,454
Nobody wants some
fresh pumpkin pie?

26
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,815
Smile.

27
00:01:44,571 --> 00:01:45,903
My children.

28
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:49,099
There are two Gothams.

29
00:01:49,343 --> 00:01:50,572
The haves.

30
00:01:51,578 --> 00:01:53,513
And the have-nots.

31
00:01:54,681 --> 00:01:56,172
I know what it is

32
00:01:57,017 --> 00:01:59,316
to feel like a have-not.

33
00:01:59,987 --> 00:02:03,617
But I say, "Enough."

34
00:02:06,593 --> 00:02:10,291
Here's to giving
the haves a taste

35
00:02:11,431 --> 00:02:13,332
of what it is like to be

36
00:02:15,002 --> 00:02:16,129
a have-not.

37
00:02:35,689 --> 00:02:36,952
Let's begin.

38
00:02:38,358 --> 00:02:39,485
Shall we?

39
00:03:02,182 --> 00:03:04,151
I'll be out of your way
in just a second, Captain.

40
00:03:04,418 --> 00:03:05,442
Harvey.

41
00:03:06,653 --> 00:03:08,451
This isn't how I wanted
things to go down.

42
00:03:08,989 --> 00:03:11,015
And yet, here we are.

43
00:03:13,026 --> 00:03:14,626
You know what I was
thinking about today?

44
00:03:15,028 --> 00:03:16,155
Our first case.

45
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:19,175
When I told you to walk
Penguin to the end of the pier,

46
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:21,862
put a bullet in his head
and dump him in the water,

47
00:03:21,935 --> 00:03:22,935
and you wouldn't.

48
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:25,269
- You thought it was wrong.
- It was.

49
00:03:25,539 --> 00:03:27,059
Well, maybe if you
would have done it,

50
00:03:27,441 --> 00:03:29,342
Falcone would still
be running things

51
00:03:29,843 --> 00:03:33,109
and a lot of people who are
dead would be alive today.

52
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,340
If I could go back,

53
00:03:35,749 --> 00:03:36,749
I'd do the same thing.

54
00:03:36,850 --> 00:03:39,376
'Cause you still don't understand
how the city works, Jim.

55
00:03:39,686 --> 00:03:41,154
You want to be a hero.

56
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,917
And Gotham doesn't need heroes.

57
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,854
It needs people who
will do what is necessary.

58
00:03:47,094 --> 00:03:49,393
You're wrong. If you
show 'em the way,

59
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:51,030
the people will follow.

60
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,158
I guess we'll just have
to wait and see, huh?

61
00:03:55,869 --> 00:03:57,132
When your leave is up,

62
00:03:57,971 --> 00:03:59,571
there'll be a desk
here waiting for you.

63
00:04:00,207 --> 00:04:01,641
Sit around, watch you all day?

64
00:04:02,442 --> 00:04:03,442
No, thanks.

65
00:04:11,785 --> 00:04:14,050
Right there's
perfect. Thank you.

66
00:04:18,925 --> 00:04:19,925
Beautiful.

67
00:04:22,229 --> 00:04:25,597
I predict this evening's fundraiser
will be a smashing success.

68
00:04:25,665 --> 00:04:27,185
If I want Gotham's
wealthiest families

69
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,759
to support the orphanage,
things have to be perfect.

70
00:04:31,138 --> 00:04:32,766
I appreciate you
taking part, Oswald.

71
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:34,774
Yes.

72
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:38,412
- Sadly, a situation has arisen.
- No.

73
00:04:39,479 --> 00:04:42,278
That thing in The Narrows
with your former chief of staff?

74
00:04:42,449 --> 00:04:44,918
No, no. This is
far more serious.

75
00:04:45,819 --> 00:04:49,153
It has to do with Mayor Burke
promoting James Gordon

76
00:04:49,256 --> 00:04:51,248
to captain of the GCPD.

77
00:04:51,825 --> 00:04:53,726
You're not really worried
about James Gordon.

78
00:04:53,794 --> 00:04:54,794
Please.

79
00:04:54,995 --> 00:04:59,126
The issue is the person
who ordered his appointment.

80
00:04:59,666 --> 00:05:00,929
- I see.
- Do you?

81
00:05:02,502 --> 00:05:05,028
Oswald, we both know
the mayor is a weasel.

82
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,504
Someone must've paid him off.

83
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,276
But I don't see why that means
you can't attend my dinner.

84
00:05:10,944 --> 00:05:13,243
Because, my dear,
the mayor has vanished.

85
00:05:13,847 --> 00:05:15,406
But I will find him.

86
00:05:15,949 --> 00:05:17,645
I will learn the
name of my enemy,

87
00:05:18,451 --> 00:05:20,283
and there will be a reckoning.

88
00:05:23,089 --> 00:05:25,456
And that is why I might not
be able to make it this evening.

89
00:05:27,727 --> 00:05:28,727
Very well,

90
00:05:29,162 --> 00:05:31,131
but a few of the
children are doing a song.

91
00:05:31,364 --> 00:05:32,696
Martin is taking part.

92
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,877
It would mean the world
to him if you could come.

93
00:05:34,901 --> 00:05:36,028
Of course.

94
00:05:38,371 --> 00:05:40,670
Now, don't let me keep you.

95
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:50,013
If you think she's the one,

96
00:05:50,717 --> 00:05:53,710
we could have
Victor talk to her.

97
00:05:55,388 --> 00:05:57,152
You do realize she is

98
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:59,520
literally my only friend.

99
00:06:00,093 --> 00:06:01,152
I need the mayor.

100
00:06:01,895 --> 00:06:02,988
I need proof.

101
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:07,665
But, sir, what if Ms.
Falcone, not to say it is her,

102
00:06:07,901 --> 00:06:10,837
has seen to it that the
mayor is missing, well,

103
00:06:11,771 --> 00:06:12,795
permanently?

104
00:06:15,842 --> 00:06:18,505
I could be chasing a ghost
while she prepares her next move.

105
00:06:20,814 --> 00:06:25,650
I wish I had a spy close
to her. Someone quiet.

106
00:06:32,125 --> 00:06:33,184
Bring me Martin.

107
00:06:34,261 --> 00:06:35,261
Who?

108
00:06:35,362 --> 00:06:36,955
The boy with the
pad around his neck.

109
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:39,563
The one who can't talk.

110
00:06:51,511 --> 00:06:53,070
I thought I was
clear. We're done.

111
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,114
<i>Penguin suspects something.</i>

112
00:06:55,849 --> 00:06:56,893
What are you talking about?

113
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:58,828
He was just here saying that
he couldn't come to the party

114
00:06:58,852 --> 00:07:00,332
I'm having tonight
for the orphanage.

115
00:07:00,654 --> 00:07:02,714
He knows someone paid the
mayor to make you captain.

116
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:04,585
<i>I think he suspects me.</i>

117
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:08,070
- Have you warned the mayor?
<i>- I'm not a fool, Jim.</i>

118
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,814
I had him leave town
after your appointment.

119
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,392
Sounds like you have your
bases covered as usual.

120
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,458
Thanks for the heads
up about Penguin.

121
00:07:15,135 --> 00:07:16,194
Don't call me again.

122
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:23,308
This is Harper.

123
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:25,606
Gordon, line one.
Says it's private.

124
00:07:29,649 --> 00:07:30,649
Sofia.

125
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:32,013
<i>Wrong. Try again.</i>

126
00:07:33,186 --> 00:07:34,279
You son of a bitch.

127
00:07:34,521 --> 00:07:36,012
Attaboy, Jim.

128
00:07:36,423 --> 00:07:37,789
Or should I say "Captain"?

129
00:07:38,158 --> 00:07:39,854
<i>Congratulations, by the way.</i>

130
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:42,422
<i>So, do you remember
when you said</i>

131
00:07:42,495 --> 00:07:45,192
the rot in Gotham
went from high to low?

132
00:07:45,765 --> 00:07:47,233
<i>You've hit the nail on the head.</i>

133
00:07:47,834 --> 00:07:50,326
Police were low,

134
00:07:51,071 --> 00:07:53,267
and now it's time
for Gotham's elite

135
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:55,105
to feel the pain.

136
00:07:56,676 --> 00:07:58,008
Enter phase two.

137
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:01,778
I won't spoil the reveal.

138
00:08:02,549 --> 00:08:05,041
Hurry outside for a little taste

139
00:08:05,618 --> 00:08:06,847
of what's to come.

140
00:08:07,487 --> 00:08:08,487
<i>Ciao, mon ami.</i>

141
00:08:11,858 --> 00:08:13,053
He's outside. Let's go.

142
00:08:14,327 --> 00:08:15,327
GCPD.

143
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:18,825
GCPD.

144
00:08:19,432 --> 00:08:20,923
Make way. GCPD.

145
00:08:21,001 --> 00:08:22,241
- Back up. Back up.
- Excuse me.

146
00:08:30,210 --> 00:08:31,439
Are they dead?

147
00:08:31,511 --> 00:08:32,672
Get forensics here.

148
00:08:33,079 --> 00:08:35,412
And I want this whole
area closed off. No press.

149
00:08:35,515 --> 00:08:37,814
That pig's eating that guy.

150
00:08:44,758 --> 00:08:46,021
Now, Harper.

151
00:08:46,926 --> 00:08:48,861
Excuse me. Excuse me.

152
00:08:58,104 --> 00:08:59,104
Where's breakfast?

153
00:09:00,173 --> 00:09:03,905
Breakfast was produced and
consumed by yours truly at breakfast time.

154
00:09:04,077 --> 00:09:07,309
It is now a fast approaching
luncheon, Master Bruce.

155
00:09:08,314 --> 00:09:09,839
Whatever. Just give me a coffee.

156
00:09:13,319 --> 00:09:14,319
Enjoying the benefits

157
00:09:14,587 --> 00:09:16,681
of another night out on
the tiles with Tommy Elliot

158
00:09:16,756 --> 00:09:18,748
and his band of
miscreants, are we?

159
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,256
How absolutely delightful.

160
00:09:25,265 --> 00:09:27,376
I know what you're going
through, you know, Master Bruce.

161
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,400
Yeah?

162
00:09:28,601 --> 00:09:30,900
I went out with my
friends. I'm hungover.

163
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:33,315
It doesn't take a
genius to figure it out.

164
00:09:33,339 --> 00:09:34,864
You're lost is what you are.

165
00:09:35,275 --> 00:09:37,642
I've seen that countless
times in young men.

166
00:09:37,877 --> 00:09:39,539
Going off to war
with a clear purpose

167
00:09:39,612 --> 00:09:42,480
only to return home to a
normal life, unable to assimilate,

168
00:09:42,649 --> 00:09:44,083
confused, angry.

169
00:09:44,884 --> 00:09:46,324
And they make a
complete tosh of it.

170
00:09:46,886 --> 00:09:48,946
I don't really care.

171
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:53,760
You killed Ra's al Ghul.

172
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,457
Vengeance for
your parents' death

173
00:09:56,563 --> 00:09:58,293
has been your driving
force for so long.

174
00:09:58,898 --> 00:10:00,457
You are completely
lost without it.

175
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:01,800
I need to call Tommy.

176
00:10:05,472 --> 00:10:07,072
Have you forgotten
what day it is today?

177
00:10:07,307 --> 00:10:09,640
- Give me my phone.
- You have, ain't you?

178
00:10:09,742 --> 00:10:11,608
Today is the day my
father took me camping.

179
00:10:11,711 --> 00:10:13,373
We put a rock on
top of Mount Bristol.

180
00:10:13,546 --> 00:10:15,742
We did it every year.
Now give me my phone.

181
00:10:25,225 --> 00:10:28,320
You are Bruce Wayne,
son of Thomas Wayne.

182
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,923
And the sooner you start
remembering that, the better.

183
00:10:32,765 --> 00:10:33,960
So, you drink your coffee,

184
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:37,931
you go upstairs, you put
your kit on 'cause you and I,

185
00:10:39,772 --> 00:10:41,001
we're going for a walk.

186
00:10:48,348 --> 00:10:50,340
According to the
medical examiner,

187
00:10:50,550 --> 00:10:53,384
both victims had been
living outdoors for some time,

188
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:54,818
most likely homeless.

189
00:10:55,021 --> 00:10:56,216
Now, see these incisions.

190
00:10:58,791 --> 00:10:59,791
He removed their organs.

191
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:01,726
- Any idea why?
- Not yet.

192
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:04,891
The Pyg all but announced
that his next victims

193
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:06,466
would be the rich and powerful.

194
00:11:06,533 --> 00:11:08,126
The high in Gotham.

195
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,962
So why is he killing
the homeless?

196
00:11:10,703 --> 00:11:13,298
You are asking for
logic from a psychopath.

197
00:11:13,373 --> 00:11:16,213
From him, yeah. Everything he's
done has been thought through carefully.

198
00:11:16,476 --> 00:11:18,707
There was a card
on the table in French.

199
00:11:19,379 --> 00:11:21,109
It said, "Long live
the revolution."

200
00:11:21,381 --> 00:11:23,646
Maybe he's using them
to make a statement.

201
00:11:25,051 --> 00:11:26,349
He wants the city's attention.

202
00:11:26,452 --> 00:11:27,452
For what?

203
00:11:28,821 --> 00:11:31,188
He said this is just a
taste of what's to come.

204
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:33,115
There's a piece
that's still missing.

205
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,788
The homeless are
densest in The Narrows

206
00:11:35,895 --> 00:11:37,022
I'm gonna start there.

207
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:38,961
A hell of a first
day to be captain.

208
00:11:39,232 --> 00:11:40,232
Yeah.

209
00:11:40,433 --> 00:11:41,793
Call me if you
find anything else.

210
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:45,848
We checked all buildings in
the three-block radius, Captain.

211
00:11:45,872 --> 00:11:46,872
Nothing.

212
00:11:47,073 --> 00:11:49,099
All right. Widen it
out a couple of blocks.

213
00:11:49,209 --> 00:11:51,440
Focus on buildings with
protected loading docks.

214
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:55,277
Captain, that was Lucius Fox.

215
00:11:56,082 --> 00:11:57,106
Final tox came back.

216
00:11:57,217 --> 00:12:00,210
Both victims had sodium sulfide
and chlorine residue on their skin.

217
00:12:00,286 --> 00:12:02,517
He says it's common
in paper manufacturing.

218
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:06,026
There's an old paper
plant a few blocks from here

219
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:08,425
that closed down a while
back. Let's check that out.

220
00:12:19,205 --> 00:12:20,725
Backup still incoming.
Should we wait?

221
00:12:20,773 --> 00:12:21,773
No.

222
00:12:24,444 --> 00:12:25,444
GORDON: Over here.

223
00:12:30,516 --> 00:12:31,516
What is he doing to them?

224
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:33,750
Taking their organs.

225
00:12:41,761 --> 00:12:42,761
HARPER: A smoker oven?

226
00:12:44,964 --> 00:12:45,964
He's cooking them.

227
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:14,626
Harper.

228
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:22,461
Drop the gun, Captain.

229
00:13:23,469 --> 00:13:24,469
Shoot this bastard.

230
00:13:24,771 --> 00:13:25,771
Drop it!

231
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:33,979
Thank you.

232
00:13:34,614 --> 00:13:38,346
You found me too soon, James.

233
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:42,653
The table is not yet set and
no meal should be served

234
00:13:43,022 --> 00:13:44,149
before its time.

235
00:13:44,791 --> 00:13:46,054
You want a hostage? Take me.

236
00:13:46,159 --> 00:13:48,151
No, no, no, no, no.
That won't do at all.

237
00:13:49,062 --> 00:13:50,792
You must see my final act.

238
00:13:52,532 --> 00:13:54,057
Along with all of Gotham!

239
00:14:12,018 --> 00:14:13,816
Right. Well, it's
a lovely day for it.

240
00:14:15,488 --> 00:14:16,488
Best foot forward.

241
00:14:21,461 --> 00:14:22,554
Very distinguished.

242
00:14:23,196 --> 00:14:25,722
Sofia tells me you're taking part
in a performance this evening.

243
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:29,860
Well, she's quite
a lady, isn't she?

244
00:14:31,371 --> 00:14:33,169
She's been a
friend to both of us.

245
00:14:35,375 --> 00:14:36,399
Or has she?

246
00:14:39,245 --> 00:14:40,245
Martin.

247
00:14:40,913 --> 00:14:44,475
I worry Sofia is only
pretending to be my friend.

248
00:14:45,251 --> 00:14:46,251
And worse,

249
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,679
I fear she may be using you.

250
00:14:55,461 --> 00:14:56,461
Now.

251
00:14:57,130 --> 00:14:59,793
I have been running
this over in my mind.

252
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:03,434
And there are two ways
this might have gone.

253
00:15:04,103 --> 00:15:07,471
One, Sofia chose a
specific orphan, you,

254
00:15:07,807 --> 00:15:10,470
to place in my path.
She groomed you,

255
00:15:11,077 --> 00:15:12,602
she told you how to act.

256
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:14,980
Or,

257
00:15:16,115 --> 00:15:18,914
Sofia simply collected
a group of children

258
00:15:19,018 --> 00:15:21,749
hoping one would gain my trust,

259
00:15:22,755 --> 00:15:24,553
and make me
easier to manipulate.

260
00:15:28,694 --> 00:15:30,629
In this version,
you are innocent.

261
00:15:36,469 --> 00:15:37,469
Martin.

262
00:15:38,471 --> 00:15:41,373
This is the version I
very badly want to believe.

263
00:15:42,809 --> 00:15:43,970
But I need proof

264
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:46,243
of our friendship.

265
00:15:46,746 --> 00:15:48,806
I need to know if my
suspicions are correct.

266
00:15:49,348 --> 00:15:51,908
And if so, what
Sofia is planning,

267
00:15:51,984 --> 00:15:53,509
and who she is planning it with.

268
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:56,449
I need you to be my
eyes and my ears.

269
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:00,532
Do you think you could do that?

270
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:10,159
Don't let me down, Martin.

271
00:16:12,004 --> 00:16:13,004
Please.

272
00:16:22,582 --> 00:16:24,517
GORDON: <i>I want a
city-wide BOLO on that van.</i>

273
00:16:24,784 --> 00:16:28,186
I want every cop in Gotham
on the streets looking for Harper.

274
00:16:28,688 --> 00:16:30,623
She will not be the
Pyg's next victim.

275
00:16:30,857 --> 00:16:31,857
- Go.
- All right.

276
00:16:31,958 --> 00:16:34,257
- All right. Let's go.
- Let's go.

277
00:16:34,927 --> 00:16:36,287
- Captain Gordon.
- Captain Gordon!

278
00:16:36,362 --> 00:16:37,796
Captain Gordon! Captain Gordon!

279
00:16:37,864 --> 00:16:40,595
Is it true that the serial killer
known as the Pyg is back?

280
00:16:40,933 --> 00:16:44,131
That he's responsible for the scene
outside the GCPD this morning?

281
00:16:44,670 --> 00:16:46,138
We believe so, yes.

282
00:16:46,205 --> 00:16:48,697
We've also heard he's
kidnapped a GCPD detective.

283
00:16:49,008 --> 00:16:50,648
How can you keep the
people of Gotham safe

284
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:52,804
when you can't protect
your own officers?

285
00:16:53,579 --> 00:16:56,674
We remain hopeful for
Detective Harper's safe return.

286
00:16:57,383 --> 00:16:58,383
Let me be clear.

287
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,812
The GCPD will stop this monster.

288
00:17:01,220 --> 00:17:03,018
- That's a promise.
- And if you fail,

289
00:17:03,089 --> 00:17:05,320
will you be pushed aside
like Harvey Bullock was?

290
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:08,440
We're done here. Thank you.

291
00:17:08,494 --> 00:17:09,587
Captain Gordon!

292
00:17:09,695 --> 00:17:13,655
What about the rumor that the
Pyg is now cooking his victims?

293
00:17:16,002 --> 00:17:17,002
Who told you that?

294
00:17:17,670 --> 00:17:18,670
Is it true?

295
00:17:20,006 --> 00:17:23,170
As I said, the GCPD will
bring the Pyg to justice.

296
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:24,476
That's all.

297
00:17:24,744 --> 00:17:27,714
Captain Gordon! Captain Gordon!

298
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,245
Someone leaked to the press
that the Pyg is cooking his victims.

299
00:17:37,156 --> 00:17:38,419
Maybe it was the Pyg.

300
00:17:39,525 --> 00:17:40,823
We know he wants attention.

301
00:17:42,261 --> 00:17:43,261
Look, Jim.

302
00:17:44,196 --> 00:17:46,062
Everyone in the
department is on your side.

303
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:48,600
Yeah.

304
00:17:49,602 --> 00:17:51,264
There is something
you need to see.

305
00:17:55,641 --> 00:17:58,372
"I grant this food will
be somewhat dear,

306
00:17:58,611 --> 00:18:01,410
"and therefore very
proper for landlords who,

307
00:18:01,881 --> 00:18:04,817
"as they have already
devoured most of the parents,

308
00:18:05,918 --> 00:18:08,444
"seem to have the
best title to the children."

309
00:18:10,222 --> 00:18:12,623
It's Jonathan Swift,
<i>A Modest Proposal.</i>

310
00:18:12,792 --> 00:18:16,388
He made an argument for cannibalism
about the rich eating the poor.

311
00:18:17,463 --> 00:18:18,829
The poor are the homeless.

312
00:18:19,465 --> 00:18:20,465
But who are the rich?

313
00:18:22,835 --> 00:18:25,031
Swift didn't just talk about
the rich eating the poor.

314
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:27,096
He specifically
mentioned the orphans.

315
00:18:29,308 --> 00:18:30,308
I know where he's going.

316
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,036
He left this for me.

317
00:18:32,244 --> 00:18:34,804
He's doing exactly what he did
with Harvey. It could be a trap.

318
00:18:36,248 --> 00:18:38,088
And I won't lead more
officers to their deaths.

319
00:18:38,317 --> 00:18:40,252
- You're going alone?
- I'm sorry, Lucius.

320
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,217
Where's Chef Louis?

321
00:18:46,993 --> 00:18:48,825
<i>Ici, mademoiselle.</i>

322
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:54,494
It's such a pleasure
to meet you in person.

323
00:18:57,169 --> 00:18:58,637
I was expecting you earlier.

324
00:18:58,704 --> 00:19:01,697
Apologies. I was detained.

325
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:04,876
But I've made a small
change in the menu.

326
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:07,477
I've steered us away
from haute cuisine

327
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:11,373
to something a bit more mundane.

328
00:19:11,951 --> 00:19:12,951
<i>Voila.</i>

329
00:19:21,193 --> 00:19:24,686
I'm calling them
Gotham meat pies.

330
00:19:26,632 --> 00:19:28,464
Your guests will die for them.

331
00:19:35,975 --> 00:19:38,638
I've made us a delicious
brown English stew

332
00:19:38,711 --> 00:19:40,373
with herb dumplings,
Master Bruce.

333
00:19:42,348 --> 00:19:44,146
Your father used to
love it when I made stew.

334
00:19:47,553 --> 00:19:50,148
Did I ever tell you how
I met your old man?

335
00:19:52,324 --> 00:19:53,324
In London.

336
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:55,855
He was doing postgrad
work there. He told me.

337
00:19:59,865 --> 00:20:01,060
Yeah, but no details.

338
00:20:03,169 --> 00:20:05,365
Well, I was just out of
the army. Two months.

339
00:20:05,604 --> 00:20:06,902
I don't remember any of it.

340
00:20:07,006 --> 00:20:09,737
All a bit of blur, really.
Booze, drugs, brawling.

341
00:20:11,377 --> 00:20:13,039
A sucking great black cloud.

342
00:20:16,115 --> 00:20:18,084
One day I wake up
and I'm lying in this alley,

343
00:20:18,184 --> 00:20:19,379
and I'm covered in blood.

344
00:20:19,852 --> 00:20:20,945
Don't know how.

345
00:20:21,454 --> 00:20:23,685
So, I picked myself up, I
took myself straight down

346
00:20:23,756 --> 00:20:25,276
to the police station,
turn myself in,

347
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:27,724
hoping that they would
chuck me into the big house

348
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,054
and throw away the key.

349
00:20:29,361 --> 00:20:31,887
And they told me to
shut up, sit down and wait.

350
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:35,997
And there was this really
annoying Yank wandering about,

351
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:37,900
dressed like he's ready
for a game of tennis,

352
00:20:38,003 --> 00:20:39,062
and it was your dad.

353
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:42,770
Anyway, he bowls up to me
and asks me what I'd done.

354
00:20:43,676 --> 00:20:44,837
Asking me questions.

355
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,902
Eventually, you know, I
found myself telling him

356
00:20:47,446 --> 00:20:49,881
stuff that I was too
frightened even to think about.

357
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:52,218
But I guess it'd
just been building.

358
00:20:53,285 --> 00:20:55,516
Anyway, at that point, the
desk sergeant called him over

359
00:20:55,588 --> 00:20:57,557
and your dad turned
around at me, and he said,

360
00:20:57,723 --> 00:21:00,784
"Alfred, last night, I was
being attacked in the alley.

361
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:03,222
"And you started
fighting this geezer.

362
00:21:03,395 --> 00:21:04,920
"I headed on my
toes, and I ran away."

363
00:21:06,332 --> 00:21:09,131
And I said, "Yeah, but that's not
what happened, is it, Thomas?"

364
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,332
And he says, "It is now."

365
00:21:15,307 --> 00:21:16,639
Your father saved my life.

366
00:21:18,744 --> 00:21:21,612
His friendship saved me.

367
00:21:23,816 --> 00:21:26,115
You see, I know what
it's all like being lonely,

368
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,652
hoping that the
world will punish you.

369
00:21:31,924 --> 00:21:32,924
I can help you.

370
00:21:38,330 --> 00:21:40,595
- Bruce, listen to me...
- Alfred, I hear you.

371
00:21:41,333 --> 00:21:43,234
I just don't want to
talk about this right now.

372
00:21:45,638 --> 00:21:46,638
All right.

373
00:21:49,074 --> 00:21:50,337
Well, this looks lovely.

374
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,842
The rocks are gone. They
must've fell out in the car.

375
00:21:57,116 --> 00:21:58,641
The keys are in
the bag, just there.

376
00:22:17,036 --> 00:22:18,334
(ENGINE STARTING)

377
00:22:29,048 --> 00:22:30,983
- Beautiful.
- So nice to see you, dear.

378
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:32,050
- Thanks.
- Yes.

379
00:22:36,388 --> 00:22:37,549
Oswald, you came!

380
00:22:38,324 --> 00:22:39,485
Look at you two.

381
00:22:39,992 --> 00:22:41,016
So handsome.

382
00:22:41,126 --> 00:22:43,527
I know how important
tonight's party is to you.

383
00:22:44,530 --> 00:22:46,158
And I wouldn't
have forgiven myself

384
00:22:46,232 --> 00:22:48,064
if I had missed
Martin's performance.

385
00:22:49,902 --> 00:22:51,530
Why don't you go
find the other children?

386
00:22:55,908 --> 00:22:57,137
Did you locate the mayor?

387
00:22:58,410 --> 00:22:59,571
Unfortunately, no.

388
00:23:00,980 --> 00:23:02,846
But I've not given up hope.

389
00:23:04,016 --> 00:23:05,096
Well, I, for one, am happy.

390
00:23:05,251 --> 00:23:06,771
This way you get to
come to my dinner.

391
00:23:08,053 --> 00:23:11,421
I need to go check on the
chef. He seems a bit odd.

392
00:23:12,458 --> 00:23:13,756
Please, try and enjoy yourself.

393
00:23:51,597 --> 00:23:52,597
Hello, Martin.

394
00:23:55,134 --> 00:23:56,134
What are you writing?

395
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:03,775
Don't make a noise.

396
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:05,076
(SHUSHING)

397
00:24:07,313 --> 00:24:09,145
I'm a cop. Who are you?

398
00:24:10,015 --> 00:24:11,278
A waiter.

399
00:24:11,483 --> 00:24:14,612
I'm looking for a man.
Caucasian, about five foot ten.

400
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:16,684
He would've brought
the food. Maybe the chef.

401
00:24:17,523 --> 00:24:18,616
The chef's in the kitchen

402
00:24:19,091 --> 00:24:20,650
Look, I just got hired tonight.

403
00:24:20,759 --> 00:24:22,270
Whatever the dude's
into, I have no idea.

404
00:24:22,294 --> 00:24:23,455
You're okay. You're okay.

405
00:24:23,862 --> 00:24:25,831
Do me a favor. Find Ms.
Falcone, bring her to me.

406
00:24:25,931 --> 00:24:27,456
- Can you do that for me?
- Yeah.

407
00:24:30,769 --> 00:24:31,849
What's that in your jacket?

408
00:24:32,838 --> 00:24:33,838
I don't...

409
00:24:39,812 --> 00:24:43,078
Jim Gordon really is an
impressive policeman.

410
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:46,342
- Was he alone?
- It seems so.

411
00:24:46,518 --> 00:24:47,645
But, man,

412
00:24:48,253 --> 00:24:49,846
whatever it is you're into,

413
00:24:49,955 --> 00:24:52,584
my partner and I,
our rates just doubled.

414
00:25:06,872 --> 00:25:07,872
(HARPER MOANING)

415
00:25:14,013 --> 00:25:15,013
Harper.

416
00:25:16,715 --> 00:25:18,809
Hi, friends. The
Falcone orphanage

417
00:25:18,984 --> 00:25:21,920
is the realization of a
long-cherished dream.

418
00:25:22,154 --> 00:25:24,180
And one that would
have not been possible

419
00:25:24,423 --> 00:25:26,915
without your support.
So, thank you.

420
00:25:27,393 --> 00:25:28,486
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

421
00:25:28,694 --> 00:25:30,405
Now, if you could please take
your seats in the next room,

422
00:25:30,429 --> 00:25:32,159
a few of the children
have prepared a song.

423
00:25:35,734 --> 00:25:36,734
Where's Martin?

424
00:25:36,935 --> 00:25:38,494
I wanted to wish him luck.

425
00:25:38,837 --> 00:25:40,499
Ah. Off getting ready, no doubt.

426
00:25:43,075 --> 00:25:44,407
Oswald, I've been thinking,

427
00:25:45,310 --> 00:25:47,142
maybe things
happened for a reason.

428
00:25:47,579 --> 00:25:49,343
Licensing crime was a bold move,

429
00:25:49,415 --> 00:25:51,247
but it would've destroyed you.

430
00:25:51,650 --> 00:25:54,518
Whoever had Jim
Gordon appointed captain,

431
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,754
may actually have saved you.

432
00:25:58,190 --> 00:26:01,160
By attempting to destroy
everything I ever created?

433
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,885
- Oswald...
- Enough!

434
00:26:03,529 --> 00:26:06,055
If you're going to
confess, confess.

435
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:08,729
And face the consequences.

436
00:26:09,001 --> 00:26:10,492
- (GUNSHOTS)
- (SCREAMING)

437
00:26:11,170 --> 00:26:13,230
So sorry to interrupt.

438
00:26:14,773 --> 00:26:17,038
The servers are
getting everyone seated.

439
00:26:17,810 --> 00:26:19,802
We don't want the
food to get cold.

440
00:26:20,646 --> 00:26:21,773
Shall we go in to dinner?

441
00:26:23,949 --> 00:26:25,212
Chop-chop.

442
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:35,660
All right.

443
00:26:35,928 --> 00:26:37,658
I stopped the bleeding, I think.

444
00:26:38,831 --> 00:26:41,071
That's the best I can do
until I can get you out of here.

445
00:26:42,601 --> 00:26:43,796
I gotta get that door open.

446
00:26:43,902 --> 00:26:45,803
- Gordon.
- Maybe I can get the hinges off.

447
00:26:45,904 --> 00:26:46,904
Gordon.

448
00:26:48,207 --> 00:26:49,573
Idiots forgot to search me.

449
00:27:08,594 --> 00:27:10,256
Is this another
one of your plans?

450
00:27:10,662 --> 00:27:11,662
No.

451
00:27:14,099 --> 00:27:17,968
Ladies and gentlemen, as
you by now have surmised,

452
00:27:18,036 --> 00:27:20,335
there's been a
change in the program.

453
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:24,838
Tonight we are proud to present

454
00:27:24,943 --> 00:27:28,607
the six merry Gothamites
of Squatter's Row

455
00:27:29,047 --> 00:27:32,040
and Martin from the
Falcone home and school

456
00:27:32,151 --> 00:27:35,644
for orphans, in our rendition of

457
00:27:36,889 --> 00:27:40,121
the meat pie tango.

458
00:27:40,192 --> 00:27:41,192
(TANGO MUSIC PLAYING)

459
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:42,386
Bob.

460
00:27:43,629 --> 00:27:44,961
Fricks.

461
00:27:46,999 --> 00:27:47,999
Trish.

462
00:27:50,135 --> 00:27:51,159
Nunuh.

463
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:54,101
Cyrano.

464
00:27:56,208 --> 00:27:57,208
Vincent.

465
00:28:01,280 --> 00:28:02,646
<i>You have it coming</i>

466
00:28:03,148 --> 00:28:04,810
<i>You have it coming</i>

467
00:28:05,117 --> 00:28:08,451
<i>You only have yourself to blame</i>

468
00:28:08,854 --> 00:28:12,552
<i>If you would've been fair
If you would've been keen</i>

469
00:28:12,724 --> 00:28:15,785
<i>I bet you these pies
Wouldn't taste the same</i>

470
00:28:16,962 --> 00:28:18,726
Enough! Where are
the other children?

471
00:28:19,231 --> 00:28:20,563
If you hurt them, I swear...

472
00:28:20,666 --> 00:28:22,032
(ALL SCREAMING)

473
00:28:24,770 --> 00:28:27,399
Rude, I'm not finished.

474
00:28:28,240 --> 00:28:29,606
Sit down.

475
00:28:31,076 --> 00:28:33,773
Pull it out, and the
next one's in her eye.

476
00:28:34,012 --> 00:28:35,012
Oswald, no.

477
00:28:35,948 --> 00:28:36,948
Don't.

478
00:28:40,953 --> 00:28:43,422
Now, to answer your
question, my dear,

479
00:28:43,522 --> 00:28:47,391
the other children and your staff
are safely locked in the kitchen.

480
00:28:48,060 --> 00:28:50,859
Despite appearances,
I am not an animal.

481
00:28:53,498 --> 00:28:56,161
Martin, may we continue?

482
00:28:59,338 --> 00:29:03,503
You have all fed upon the
poor of Gotham for years.

483
00:29:03,842 --> 00:29:06,209
Now, you're going to
know what they taste like.

484
00:29:07,012 --> 00:29:10,608
Please open your envelopes
and look at the photographs inside.

485
00:29:13,185 --> 00:29:14,517
Come on.

486
00:29:15,554 --> 00:29:16,554
Open them!

487
00:29:25,664 --> 00:29:26,996
Who is Trish?

488
00:29:27,633 --> 00:29:29,727
Well, I thought you should
see who you are eating.

489
00:29:31,903 --> 00:29:36,568
Bob, Fricks, Trish,
Nunuh, Cyrano, and Vincent

490
00:29:36,642 --> 00:29:39,111
all deserve our gratitude.

491
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:42,243
So, these pies are...

492
00:29:42,414 --> 00:29:44,781
People. Yup,
they're people pies.

493
00:29:45,017 --> 00:29:46,017
People.

494
00:29:48,420 --> 00:29:49,979
And you're all
going to eat them.

495
00:29:50,422 --> 00:29:51,788
(ALL GROAN IN DISGUST)

496
00:29:52,224 --> 00:29:55,285
Absolutely not.

497
00:29:55,927 --> 00:29:56,927
Okay.

498
00:30:01,600 --> 00:30:03,091
Let's try this again.

499
00:30:03,168 --> 00:30:04,168
No!

500
00:30:04,736 --> 00:30:06,932
Eat, or I kill the boy.

501
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:09,768
But he's just an orphan.

502
00:30:12,744 --> 00:30:13,744
What did you say?

503
00:30:14,012 --> 00:30:16,777
Well, these are made
of people, for God's sake.

504
00:30:16,848 --> 00:30:18,680
You can't expect us, I mean...

505
00:30:19,017 --> 00:30:20,508
So they kill some urchin.

506
00:30:27,526 --> 00:30:29,154
What a waste of a good pie.

507
00:30:31,163 --> 00:30:33,064
But I do applaud the sentiment.

508
00:30:33,298 --> 00:30:36,735
Especially, as you, Mr. Cobblepot,
are the reason I'm here.

509
00:30:37,469 --> 00:30:39,165
Me? Why?

510
00:30:39,571 --> 00:30:42,973
I could've chosen any
gathering of wealthy Gothamites

511
00:30:43,408 --> 00:30:46,071
who've gotten fat
upon the poor, but you,

512
00:30:46,812 --> 00:30:49,179
with your Pax Penguina,

513
00:30:49,414 --> 00:30:51,679
you are the biggest
glutton of them all.

514
00:30:51,850 --> 00:30:54,479
You have gorged
yourself on this city's heart,

515
00:30:54,553 --> 00:30:56,613
its lungs, its liver.

516
00:30:57,489 --> 00:30:59,014
Why should today
be any different?

517
00:30:59,791 --> 00:31:02,556
Now, eat, little penguin. Eat.

518
00:31:03,795 --> 00:31:05,661
Eat the pies or the boy dies.

519
00:31:26,852 --> 00:31:28,184
(RETCHING)

520
00:31:33,425 --> 00:31:34,757
If you don't all eat,

521
00:31:34,860 --> 00:31:38,456
I will hunt you
down and kill you all!

522
00:31:44,136 --> 00:31:47,106
Now, that's what I like to see.

523
00:31:58,417 --> 00:32:00,943
And as mother
always used to say,

524
00:32:01,286 --> 00:32:04,620
"Nobody leaves until
every plate is clean."

525
00:32:04,890 --> 00:32:07,883
It's a compliment to the
chef. And I love compliments.

526
00:32:10,362 --> 00:32:11,591
And Ms. Falcone...

527
00:32:15,434 --> 00:32:18,427
<i>Mangia, signorina.</i>

528
00:32:21,306 --> 00:32:22,433
Only if you don't hurt him.

529
00:32:36,021 --> 00:32:37,182
Can you help me?

530
00:32:44,496 --> 00:32:45,496
Yes.

531
00:32:50,202 --> 00:32:51,202
(GROANS)

532
00:33:13,859 --> 00:33:15,122
No!

533
00:33:16,528 --> 00:33:17,757
He'll kill the kid!

534
00:33:17,929 --> 00:33:18,929
Get off of me!

535
00:33:19,998 --> 00:33:20,998
Martin!

536
00:33:22,701 --> 00:33:23,701
Jim!

537
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,015
Get out of here!

538
00:33:38,850 --> 00:33:39,850
Go!

539
00:34:21,726 --> 00:34:22,726
Come on, Jim.

540
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:24,428
Don't give up.

541
00:34:24,696 --> 00:34:26,096
You will ruin everything.

542
00:34:40,946 --> 00:34:41,946
Should be better.

543
00:34:50,622 --> 00:34:51,622
How is your hand?

544
00:34:52,924 --> 00:34:53,924
I'll be fine.

545
00:34:54,326 --> 00:34:55,326
How's Martin?

546
00:34:56,094 --> 00:34:57,494
He's stronger than he looks.

547
00:35:02,601 --> 00:35:04,797
You paid off the mayor to
make Jim Gordon captain.

548
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,105
Yes.

549
00:35:10,141 --> 00:35:13,305
And you want me to believe
that you did this out of friendship.

550
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:16,539
To save me.

551
00:35:18,583 --> 00:35:20,643
I tried to talk you out
of the license program,

552
00:35:20,752 --> 00:35:21,879
you wouldn't listen.

553
00:35:23,288 --> 00:35:24,779
There seemed no other way.

554
00:35:28,627 --> 00:35:32,758
Of course, it's equally
plausible that you are my enemy

555
00:35:33,965 --> 00:35:35,524
intent upon my destruction.

556
00:35:37,602 --> 00:35:39,093
You could choose
to see it that way.

557
00:35:39,804 --> 00:35:41,170
The choice is yours, Oswald.

558
00:35:41,473 --> 00:35:42,473
Well,

559
00:35:43,375 --> 00:35:45,310
whatever your actual reasoning,

560
00:35:48,046 --> 00:35:49,537
you went behind my back.

561
00:35:51,783 --> 00:35:53,445
I would be justified
in killing you.

562
00:36:00,892 --> 00:36:02,884
But what you were
going to do for Martin,

563
00:36:07,265 --> 00:36:08,265
that was real.

564
00:36:12,604 --> 00:36:13,936
Don't ever betray me again.

565
00:36:16,374 --> 00:36:17,374
Never.

566
00:36:20,111 --> 00:36:21,340
I will abandon the licenses.

567
00:36:22,514 --> 00:36:24,380
But Jim Gordon
cannot be captain.

568
00:36:25,383 --> 00:36:26,510
Pick someone else then.

569
00:36:26,851 --> 00:36:28,285
Gordon's less
than nothing to me.

570
00:36:40,899 --> 00:36:42,561
Oh, my God, look!

571
00:36:42,667 --> 00:36:44,932
- It's the Pyg!
- It's the Pyg!

572
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:46,537
It's really him.

573
00:36:48,907 --> 00:36:51,433
CROWD: Bye,
bye, piggy, bye, bye.

574
00:36:52,343 --> 00:36:53,888
- REPORTER 1: Captain Gordon!
- REPORTER 2: Captain Gordon!

575
00:36:53,912 --> 00:36:55,222
- Captain Gordon!
- Captain Gordon!

576
00:36:55,246 --> 00:36:57,044
- Captain Gordon!
- Captain Gordon!

577
00:36:58,950 --> 00:36:59,950
Is that the Pyg?

578
00:37:00,285 --> 00:37:01,378
Did you really catch him?

579
00:37:02,954 --> 00:37:05,253
The suspect known
as the Pyg is in custody.

580
00:37:05,857 --> 00:37:08,691
Detective Vanessa Harper is
on her way to Gotham General

581
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,995
and is expected to
make a full recovery.

582
00:37:13,498 --> 00:37:15,160
The GCPD kept its promise.

583
00:37:18,837 --> 00:37:19,837
Captain Gordon.

584
00:37:20,438 --> 00:37:21,438
Yes?

585
00:37:22,107 --> 00:37:23,107
Thank you.

586
00:37:23,942 --> 00:37:24,942
Thank you.

587
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:47,895
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

588
00:37:53,571 --> 00:37:54,595
Come on.

589
00:37:58,910 --> 00:38:00,435
Hey, Alfred!

590
00:38:02,914 --> 00:38:03,914
How was your walk?

591
00:38:05,150 --> 00:38:06,174
Everybody out now.

592
00:38:07,018 --> 00:38:08,018
Nobody move.

593
00:38:09,954 --> 00:38:10,978
This is not your house.

594
00:38:12,223 --> 00:38:14,023
If I want my friends
to stay, they're staying.

595
00:38:18,830 --> 00:38:19,830
Like hell they are.

596
00:38:19,931 --> 00:38:21,661
Dude, your butler
is a little out of line.

597
00:38:23,735 --> 00:38:25,727
Have you been hitting
the sherry, Jeeves?

598
00:38:25,804 --> 00:38:29,241
You have no idea what extreme
danger you are now in, son.

599
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:30,639
If I was you, I would walk away.

600
00:38:32,644 --> 00:38:33,644
Yeah, whatever.

601
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:36,406
Meet us at the club.

602
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:40,247
Come on, driver will take us.

603
00:38:50,728 --> 00:38:51,728
Well, you...

604
00:38:55,834 --> 00:38:57,645
You certainly showed a
new side of yourself today

605
00:38:57,669 --> 00:38:59,509
- haven't you, Master Bruce?
- Save it, Alfred.

606
00:39:00,338 --> 00:39:01,670
You tell me a story

607
00:39:01,973 --> 00:39:04,568
about you and my Dad, and
I'm supposed to get all weepy.

608
00:39:08,079 --> 00:39:09,672
You don't know what
I'm going through.

609
00:39:12,116 --> 00:39:13,482
You and I are nothing alike.

610
00:39:14,385 --> 00:39:15,385
Then talk to me.

611
00:39:17,222 --> 00:39:19,487
Let me know how I can help you.

612
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:20,691
You can't!

613
00:39:22,493 --> 00:39:24,325
Like you said, I did what I did.

614
00:39:26,231 --> 00:39:27,392
I killed Ra's.

615
00:39:28,633 --> 00:39:31,228
I avenged my parents'
death, and guess what?

616
00:39:33,705 --> 00:39:34,705
Nothing changed.

617
00:39:38,877 --> 00:39:40,402
It made no difference.

618
00:39:41,012 --> 00:39:42,480
So then what did I do it for?

619
00:39:48,219 --> 00:39:49,346
How can you help that?

620
00:39:50,788 --> 00:39:52,586
I can help with the
way that you're feeling.

621
00:39:55,226 --> 00:39:56,455
But you need to talk to me.

622
00:39:59,364 --> 00:40:01,595
You have to face up
to who you really are.

623
00:40:01,699 --> 00:40:03,065
Stop telling me who I am.

624
00:40:05,603 --> 00:40:06,696
I know who I am.

625
00:40:09,807 --> 00:40:11,275
And if you really
want to help me,

626
00:40:12,577 --> 00:40:15,672
you can stop trying to be my
father, and you can be my butler.

627
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:18,081
Clean this place up.

628
00:40:21,419 --> 00:40:22,443
Tommy!

629
00:40:45,176 --> 00:40:46,474
You're the hero of the day.

630
00:40:47,745 --> 00:40:48,906
I was just doing my job.

631
00:40:49,247 --> 00:40:51,773
I know you hate
me for what I did,

632
00:40:51,849 --> 00:40:53,283
but you deserve to be captain.

633
00:40:53,751 --> 00:40:54,991
I went to your father for help,

634
00:40:55,420 --> 00:40:56,683
I knew what I was getting into.

635
00:40:57,789 --> 00:40:59,149
It doesn't mean
I have to like it.

636
00:40:59,757 --> 00:41:00,757
But you accept it.

637
00:41:03,695 --> 00:41:05,186
Because I do deserve it.

638
00:41:06,798 --> 00:41:08,858
Just like Gotham
deserves law and order.

639
00:41:10,268 --> 00:41:11,793
And I'm gonna
make sure it gets it.

640
00:41:14,205 --> 00:41:15,673
You don't think
I want that, too?

641
00:41:19,010 --> 00:41:20,239
I'm not your enemy, Jim.

642
00:41:21,446 --> 00:41:22,446
I never will be.

643
00:41:58,750 --> 00:42:00,218
Did you find anything out?

644
00:42:06,491 --> 00:42:07,491
"I saw Sofia

645
00:42:08,026 --> 00:42:10,154
"kissing the policeman."

646
00:42:15,333 --> 00:42:16,333
Is this true?

647
00:42:45,696 --> 00:42:47,392
Martin, you are a good friend.

648
00:42:53,037 --> 00:42:54,037
As for Sofia,

649
00:42:56,808 --> 00:42:58,743
she will answer
for what she's done.

650
00:43:01,245 --> 00:43:02,269
I swear.

651
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:16,326
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

652
00:43:47,258 --> 00:43:48,258
English Template
